From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: sfp: support shared (non-exclusive) mod-def0 GPIOs

The BPI-R4 Pro routes each SFP cage's MOD-DEF0 presence line to two
consumers: the sfp core, and the ethernet lane-mux workers that select
between the cage and an optional copper PHY based on module presence.
Request mod-def0 with GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE so both can hold
the same GPIO.

The sfp core then trips over its own request flags: the probe IRQ
loop and sfp_gpio_get_state() compare gpio_flags[i] against GPIOD_IN
with an exact match, so the NONEXCLUSIVE bit made sfp skip both the
mod-def0 IRQ request and the presence read -- module insertion was
never detected.  Mask GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE off before the
comparison.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
index f77b84c1e8c5..27889bc2d44c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ static const char *gpio_names[] = {
 };
 
 static const enum gpiod_flags gpio_flags[] = {
-	GPIOD_IN,
+	GPIOD_IN | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE,
 	GPIOD_IN,
 	GPIOD_IN,
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
@@ -163,6 +163,12 @@ static const enum gpiod_flags gpio_flags[] = {
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
 };
 
+static bool sfp_gpio_is_input(unsigned int gpio)
+{
+	return (gpio_flags[gpio] & (GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_DIR_SET |
+				    GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_DIR_OUT)) == GPIOD_IN;
+}
+
 /* t_start_up (SFF-8431) or t_init (SFF-8472) is the time required for a
  * non-cooled module to initialise its laser safety circuitry. We wait
  * an initial T_WAIT period before we check the tx fault to give any PHY
@@ -656,7 +662,7 @@ static unsigned int sfp_gpio_get_state(struct sfp *sfp)
 	unsigned int i, state, v;
 
 	for (i = state = 0; i < GPIO_MAX; i++) {
-		if (gpio_flags[i] != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
+		if (!sfp_gpio_is_input(i) || !sfp->gpio[i])
 			continue;
 
 		v = gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[i]);
@@ -1992,7 +1998,7 @@ static int sfp_sm_probe_phy(struct sfp *sfp, int addr, bool is_c45)
 	/* Mark this PHY as being on a SFP module */
 	phy->is_on_sfp_module = true;
 
-	err = phy_device_register_locked(phy);
+	err = phy_device_register(phy);
 	if (err) {
 		phy_device_free(phy);
 		dev_err(sfp->dev, "phy_device_register failed: %pe\n",
@@ -3272,7 +3278,7 @@ static int sfp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < GPIO_MAX; i++) {
-		if (gpio_flags[i] != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
+		if (!sfp_gpio_is_input(i) || !sfp->gpio[i])
 			continue;
 
 		sfp->gpio_irq[i] = gpiod_to_irq(sfp->gpio[i]);
